      considerations: [
        'Win exactly the number of tricks you bid each hand. Score 5 plus tricks made when you make your contract; lose 1 point per trick over or under your bid. Highest total score after the full deal sequence wins.',
        "Each hand: dealer deals the current hand size (1 to 8 cards per player). Next card is turned for trump (except in 8-card hands, which are no-trump). In order from dealer's left, each player bids how many tricks they will take; the sum of all bids must not equal the number of cards per player. Player to dealer's left leads; follow suit if possible, otherwise play trump if possible, else discard. Highest trump wins the trick, or highest card of the led suit if no trump. Trick winner leads. After all tricks are played, score: make contract = 5 + tricks made; miss = minus 1 per trick difference.",
        'Bid exact number of tricks; sum of all bids must not equal cards per player.',
        'Follow suit; if unable, must trump if possible; else discard any card.',
      ],
